# Vauxhall A-type 20 hp tourer, 1908-1914.
#
# The A-type IS the 20 hp car announced in October 1908, not a model that
# preceded it: the car it was developed from was the 12/16 hp X-type. It was
# built as the A09, A11 and A12, with a 16-20 hp variant, and the 1912 A12
# cabriolet with its hood raised is the body modelled. Late cars were
# assembled into 1915.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_A-type
#
# Dimensions: wheelbase 2.921 m or 3.124 m (115 or 123 in). No overall length,
# width or height was published, so the overall length is measured from the
# photograph and the width and height are estimated; the estimates are
# recorded rather than presented as factory figures.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a period halftone print, near-level within about
# 5-10 degrees, camera at hub height; it is not a modern photograph and only
# 960 px was obtainable.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Vauxhall colour list was found. Black, Dark Green,
# Maroon and Grey are period finishes. Weights 10, 9, 8, 7, total 34,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 100 km/h. Comfort 20/360, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 20. Classes 2,3.
# Dates: intro October 1908; retires staggered 1928-1932 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-a-type.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-a-type.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-a-type/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the overall dimensions, the radiator face, the lamp
# arrangement and the rear closure are inferred, there being no front or rear
# photograph of this body. The hood framing is simplified, and the halftone
# does not establish a paint colour.


obj=citycar
